K4-R3 F3 Fix Verification: switch_to TSS.rsp0 & CR3 Reload
==========================================================
Task: A2.4 K4-R3 F3 (docs/queue-2026-11-03.md)
Reviewed finding: docs/reviews/k4-r3-freebuff.log F3
Date: 2026-11-03
Agent: antigravity

1. Code Changes
---------------
- In `kernel/src/gdt.rs`:
  Added public accessor `pub fn get_tss_rsp0() -> u64` reading `TSS.rsp0` from the
  active Task State Segment struct.
- In `kernel/src/proc.rs`:
  In `proc::switch_to(pid)`:
  Reload `TSS.rsp0` with `proc.kstack_top` via `crate::gdt::set_tss_rsp0(proc.kstack_top)`
  whenever `proc.kstack_top != 0`, in addition to reloading CR3 with `proc.cr3` and
  updating `CURRENT_PID`.
- In `kernel/src/trustselftest.rs`:
  Added a committed two-process context switch test:
  - Takes PID 1 (`novad`) and PID 2 (`bad_mem`), verifying they have distinct, non-zero
    page tables (`cr3`) and kernel stacks (`kstack_top`).
  - Calls `proc::switch_to(PID_NOVAD)`:
    Asserts `proc::current_pid() == PID_NOVAD`, live hardware `current_cr3() == p1.cr3`,
    and live hardware `get_tss_rsp0() == p1.kstack_top`.
  - Calls `proc::switch_to(pid2)`:
    Asserts `proc::current_pid() == pid2`, live hardware `current_cr3() == p2.cr3`,
    and live hardware `get_tss_rsp0() == p2.kstack_top`.
  - Calls `proc::switch_to(PID_KERNEL)`:
    Asserts `proc::current_pid() == PID_KERNEL` and live hardware `current_cr3() == kernel_pml4`.

